    },
    "message": "Narrow intervention target zones by the scenario data\n\nAdditions without a named zone asked about every zone. The rule parser now\noffers the zones the data ties to the operation: toilets where toilets\nare, arrivals where people are received, staff where staff are stationed,\ndepartures where evacuees are; one such zone is chosen and the choice is\na plan assumption. \"トイレゾーン\" names the toilet zone. The compiler\nsummary gives each zone's staff and evacuee counts. When Opus asks which\nzone and the rules settle it, the rule plan is used, and Opus choices must\nbe IDs of one target kind. The project screen shows choices as buttons\nthat add a zone_id line and preview again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
